WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.060
- Hannah Gutierrez Reed finally speaks out

00:00:02.060 --> 00:00:04.700
through her lawyers about her
involvement or lack thereof

00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:07.300
in the death of Halyna
Hutchins on the set of Rust.

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:09.090
She claims that it was sabotage.

00:00:09.090 --> 00:00:10.670
Now this allegation or speculation

00:00:10.670 --> 00:00:12.760
probably doesn't change
anything on the video I did

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:14.450
regarding the whole shooting situation,

00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:16.100
but there are a couple
of interesting wrinkles.

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:16.933
Number one,

00:00:16.933 --> 00:00:20.080
if someone did intentionally
put a live round into the gun,

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:22.060
that would almost certainly
qualify as what's called

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:23.520
depraved heart murder.

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:25.210
Effectively, that person
would have engaged

00:00:25.210 --> 00:00:27.670
in an act that was wildly reckless,

00:00:27.670 --> 00:00:30.850
and very likely to end up
hurting or killing someone

00:00:30.850 --> 00:00:33.600
and that is often grounds for
murder in the second degree.

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:35.840
Number two, this probably
doesn't help Ms. Gutierrez Reed

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:37.370
if it's her job to check the gun

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:39.890
and check every round
before it's used in a scene,

00:00:39.890 --> 00:00:41.490
the fact that someone
intentionally put it there,

00:00:41.490 --> 00:00:43.880
doesn't obviate the need
to actually go through

00:00:43.880 --> 00:00:45.390
and check every single round.

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:47.150
Maybe it would help if
someone added the round

00:00:47.150 --> 00:00:48.480
after she had checked the gun,

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:50.360
but then that raises
questions of chain of custody.

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:53.160
Why was the gun in such a place
that it allowed someone else

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:55.880
to put that round in
outside of her supervision?

00:00:55.880 --> 00:00:57.270
So this is interesting speculation,

00:00:57.270 --> 00:01:00.103
but probably not the legal
defense that she thinks it is.

